    <statement><p>Evaluate the indefinite integral.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle\int x^{7}\cos\mathopen{}\left(x^{4}\right) \, dx</m>
             = <fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0001"/> <m>+ C</m>.</p>
<p><B> Hint:</B>
First make a substitution and then use integration by parts to evaluate the integral.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{1}{4}x^{4}\sin\mathopen{}\left(x^{4}\right)+\frac{1}{4}\cos\mathopen{}\left(x^{4}\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
